<title>DENMARK: Unidanmark sees lower Danish 1997 c/a surplus.</title>
<headline>Unidanmark sees lower Danish 1997 c/a surplus.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey Denmark's second biggest bank Unidanmark on Tuesday lowered its forecast for Denmark's 1997 current account surplus to 9.0 billion crowns from 11.0 billion crowns in its last forecast in June.</p>
<p>At the same time it left unchanged its estimate for this year's GDP (gross domestic product) growth at 3.2 percent, cutting its inflation rate forecast to 2.2 percent from 2.3 percent.</p>
